From 72e032ac6e74250dae781eeed4a7e3298edcaef6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teresa Johnson <tejohnson@google.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:57:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Bitcode] Assign GUIDs when reading bitcode that predates
 !guid metadata (#238614)

Enable backwards compatibility with legacy bitcode as required for LLVM.
Bitcode produced before #184065 has no !guid metadata, so loading it
into LTO leaves definitions without a GUID. Regular LTO then asserts in
GlobalValue::getGUID() once an internal symbol is promoted and renamed
(e.g. WPD on vf.llvm.merged), and the ThinLTO backend silently skips
dropping dead symbols.

Fix this as a bitcode upgrade so that regular LTO, in-process and
distributed ThinLTO, and libLTO are all covered without touching LTO or
IRMover. When no MODULE_CODE_GUIDLIST record is seen, compute each
definition's GUID from its original name and linkage at load time and
record it in the module's value-to-GUID map. The !guid metadata is
attached when it becomes legal: for globals when module metadata is
materialized, and for functions when their body is. This matches what
AssignGUIDPass would have produced when the bitcode was written.

Current writers always emit MODULE_CODE_GUIDLIST, even when empty, so
llvm-as | llvm-dis round trips of IR without !guid are unchanged. Only
tests that disassemble checked-in legacy .bc files see new !guid
attachments; their CHECK lines are updated.

Assisted-by: Gemini
